# local-only scratch — never committed; safe place for personal files,
# experiments, and anything that should never reach the repo
.local/

# AI tooling — local by default; opt in specific shareable artifacts below.
#
# `.claude/skills/` is broadly tracked (production-skill convention from
# PR #104). New skills land in git unless explicitly re-ignored.
#
# `.claude/agent-verdicts/` is per-file because most entries are local-only
# reasoning. Anything cited as a `receipt.path` in the skill-registry JSON
# MUST be opted in below so the link resolves on GitHub:
#  - `SKILL-REGISTRY-*` — registry docs (verdict + dated JSON + LATEST.json)
#  - `SKILL-USAGE-*` — transcript-measured usage (dated JSON + LATEST.json);
#    consumed by /skill-registry's transcript-measurement overlay so the
#    measurement file has to travel with the repo, not just live on one
#    developer's machine
#  - `README-SYNC-AGENT.md` — token-economics receipt for /sync-readmes
# Other skills that should ship their docs add a
# `!.claude/agent-verdicts/<FILE>` line of their own.
#
# Everything else (settings, worktrees, transcripts) stays local.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/agent-verdicts/
.claude/agent-verdicts/*
!.claude/agent-verdicts/SKILL-REGISTRY-*
!.claude/agent-verdicts/SKILL-USAGE-*
!.claude/agent-verdicts/SKILL-CALIBRATION-*
!.claude/agent-verdicts/README-SYNC-AGENT.md
.cursor/
.aider*
.continue/
.windsurf/

# Local-only cache for scripts/ (e.g. bucket-review-invocations.py's PR-size
# lookups). Grows as new PRs are queried; not useful to commit because each
# developer's local /review usage targets a different set of PRs.
.cache/

# playwright e2e
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
